%p
  Hello #{@teacher.name},
%p
  We noticed that you haven't logged in to your Code.org account in over 3 years. To keep our systems secure and up-to-date, we regularly delete accounts that have been inactive for this long.
%h3
  What's happening?
%p
  Your account is scheduled for deletion in 30 days due to 3 years of inactivity.
%h3
  How to keep your account:
%p
  If you'd like to keep your Code.org account active, simply log in at any time within the next 30 days. This will automatically prevent your account from being deleted.
%h3
  What if you miss the 30-day deadline?
%p
  If your account is deleted after 30 days, you can still contact Code.org Support to recover your account—but only for the next 28 days. After that period, your account and all associated personal data will be permanently deleted and cannot be recovered.
  If you have any questions or need help, please reply to this email or reach out to
  %a{href:SharedConstants::EMAIL_LINKS.CDO_SUPPORT_MAILTO}support@code.org.
%p
  Thank you,
%p
  The Code.org Team
